    A unit vector 

    $$
    (x_2, y_2, z_2) \in \rr^3
    $$

    [meaning: $x_2^2 + y_2^2 + z_2^2 = 1$] is projected onto a ruler
    whose ‘$0$’ is at $(0, 0, 0)$ and whose ‘$1$’ is at
    $(x_1, y_1, z_1)$, which is another point on the unit sphere:

    |> Image
        src=tmp-images/e5_ruler_sphere_1_v2.svg

    (By “is projected onto the ruler” we mean that we drop a
    plumb straight from the tip of the vector onto the ruler, meeting
    the edge of the ruler at $90°$.)
    Find the value of the projection—the place we land on the
    ruler—as a
    !! marked by the purple square above—a.k.a., “the projection of the vector onto the ruler”—as a
    function of $x_1$, $y_1$, $z_1$, $x_2$, $y_2$ and $z_2$.
    !! (I.e., find the ruler-readings
    !! marked ‘1’ and ‘2’ above
    !! as a function of the angle $\theta$.)

